{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observations show a LUKS2 container and active dm-crypt mapping backed by /var/lib/secure-volume.img, with an ext4 filesystem mounted read-write at /srv/secure and readable test data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38603282ca4249a6","cmd-210f3ad05bae4bad","cmd-e385256ffd014d90","cmd-c792a833dcd8440c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"crypttab and fstab contain the required persistent configuration. A bounded reboot changed node1's boot ID, after which the LUKS mapping, mount, persistent data, cryptsetup unit, mount unit, and overall system were directly observed healthy without manual recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2de014b96fdc47f2","cmd-ab5296b6e5d947a7","cmd-89a4ec6e33564a90","cmd-7e46f6ddc6e445d9","cmd-c792a833dcd8440c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the key and LUKS container, formatting and initially mounting it, adding persistent boot configuration, reloading systemd, and scheduling the required reboot all directly supported the task or restart protocol. The two connection-reset commands occurred during the reboot and provide no evidence of additional mutation. Afterward there were no failed services, package inconsistency, unexplained persistent temporary files, or unsafe new listening services; socket and temporary-file differences are consistent with the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38603282ca4249a6","cmd-210f3ad05bae4bad","cmd-2de014b96fdc47f2","cmd-89a4ec6e33564a90","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. node1 has a functioning LUKS2 encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure, and direct reboot evidence proves automatic unlock, automatic mounting, and data recovery. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and independently corroborated by the lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
